1ec:[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"11\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/tools-web-restrictions\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Restrict web search and web fetch domains\"]}]\n1ee:[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"6\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/browser-use-sdk\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Browser and computer use with the SDK toolsets\"]}]\n1ef:[\"$\",\"li\",\"9\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"0\",{\"id\":\"october-7-2026-3\",\"children\":\"$undefined\"}],\"Claude Max, Ultra, and Team plans now include monthly API credits. To learn how to claim them, see \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"2\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/about-claude/api-credits-for-subscribers\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"API credits for Max, Ultra, and Team plans\"]}],\".\"]}]\n1f0:[\"$\",\"li\",\"11\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"0\",{\"id\":\"october-7-2026-5\",\"children\":\"$undefined\"}],\"In Claude Managed Agents, a cloud environment with \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"limited\"]}],\" networking now also applies its \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"4\",{\"children\":[\"allowed_hosts\"]}],\" to the \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"6\",{\"children\":[\"web_search\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"8\",{\"children\":[\"web_fetch\"]}],\" tools. A \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"10\",{\"children\":[\"web_fetch\"]}],\" call for a URL on a host that \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"12\",{\"children\":[\"allowed_hosts\"]}],\" does not match returns a \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"14\",{\"children\":[\"url_not_allowed\"]}],\" error result to the agent. \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"16\",{\"children\":[\"web_search\"]}],\" omits results from such hosts. When \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"18\",{\"children\":[\"allowed_hosts\"]}],\" lists no hosts, neither tool returns a page or a search result. \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"20\",{\"children\":[\"allow_package_managers\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"22\",{\"children\":[\"allow_mcp_servers\"]}],\" add no hosts for these tools. To let the tools reach a host, add it to \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"24\",{\"children\":[\"allowed_hosts\"]}],\", which also opens it to the sandbox. \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"26\",{\"children\":[\"unrestricted\"]}],\" networking and self-hosted environments do not limit these tools. See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"28\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/environments#networking\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Environment networking\"]}],\".\"]}]\n1f1:[\"$\",\"li\",\"13\",{\"children\":[\"With \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"1\",{\"children\":[\"limited\"]}],\" networking, creating a session fails with a 400 error when an enabled web tool’s \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"allowed_domains\"]}],\" has an entry not within \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"allowed_hosts\"]}],\". So does a session update that adds such an entry. An \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"7\",{\"children\":[\"allowed_hosts\"]}],\" entry matches one exact host unless it starts with \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"9\",{\"children\":[\"*.\"]}],\", so \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"11\",{\"children\":[\"docs.example.com\"]}],\" is not within \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"13\",{\"children\":[\"[\\\"example.com\\\"]\"]}],\". To fix the error, add the host to \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"15\",{\"children\":[\"allowed_hosts\"]}],\" or remove the entry from \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"17\",{\"children\":[\"allowed_domains\"]}],\". See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"19\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/tools-web-restrictions\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Restrict web search and web fetch domains\"]}],\".\"]}]\n1f2:[\"$\",\"li\",\"15\",{\"children\":[\"In Claude Managed Agents, the \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/tools#available-tools\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"web_fetch\"]}],\" tool\"]}],\" now fetches only URLs that have already appeared in the session, for example in the text of a user message, in a \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"web_search\"]}],\" result, or in a page that \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"web_fetch\"]}],\" returned earlier. This reduces the risk of data exfiltration. A URL that appears only in Claude’s own output, the agent’s system prompt, an attached document, or the output of a tool such as \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"7\",{\"children\":[\"bash\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"9\",{\"children\":[\"read\"]}],\", or an MCP tool does not count: a \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"11\",{\"children\":[\"web_fetch\"]}],\" call for it returns a \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"13\",{\"children\":[\"url_not_in_prior_context\"]}],\" error result to the agent. To let the agent fetch a URL, send it in the text of a \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"15\",{\"children\":[\"user.message\"]}],\" event.\"]}]\n1f6:[\"$\",\"code\",\"13\",{\"children\":[\"mcp_tool_listing\"]}]\n1f7:[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"13\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking#preserved-thinking\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Preserved thinking\"]}]\n1f8:[\"$\",\"li\",\"9\",{\"children\":[\"Per-message effort changes are in beta on Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5.1, and Claude Opus 5 on the Claude API. Add a \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"1\",{\"children\":[\"role: \\\"system\\\"\"]}],\" message with \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"output_config.effort\"]}],\" inside \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"messages\"]}],\" to change effort for later turns while preserving the prompt cache. Include the \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"7\",{\"children\":[\"mid-conversation-output-config-2026-07-01\"]}],\" beta header in your requests. See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"9\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/build-with-claude/effort#change-effort-mid-conversation-beta\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Per-message effort\"]}],\".\"]}]\n1f9:[\"$\",\"li\",\"11\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"0\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/build-with-claude/mid-conversation-system-messages#turn-scoped-system-messages\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Turn-scoped system messages\"]}],\" are in beta (\",[\"$\",\"code\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21\"]}],\" header). Set \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"4\",{\"children\":[\"clear_at: \\\"next_user_message\\\"\"]}],\" on a mid-conversation \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"6\",{\"children\":[\"role: \\\"system\\\"\"]}],\" message and it renders for the current turn only, then stays in the history at no token cost. Per-turn reminders don’t accumulate and don’t invalidate the prompt cache or later thinking blocks.\"]}]\n1fa:[\"$\",\"li\",\"13\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"thinking.display\"]}],\" accepts a third value, \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"\\\"updates\\\"\"]}],\", in beta (\",[\"$\",\"code\",\"4\",{\"children\":[\"thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18\"]}],\" header). Reasoning comes back with an empty \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"6\",{\"children\":[\"thinking\"]}],\" field, as under \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"8\",{\"children\":[\"\\\"omitted\\\"\"]}],\", and the short progress updates that Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5.1, and Claude Fable 5 write between tool calls come back as text, at most one \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"10\",{\"children\":[\"thinking\"]}],\" block before a tool call. See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"12\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking#progress-updates\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Progress updates between tool calls\"]}],\".\"]}]\n1fb:[\"$\",\"li\",\"15\",{\"children\":[\"Text generated by Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1 carries Anthropic’s text watermark, and supported image, video, and audio files that Claude produces through the \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/code-execution-tool\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"code execution tool\"]}],\" carry C2PA Content Credentials when you retrieve them through the \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/build-with-claude/files\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Files API\"]}],\" on the Claude API. Marking requires no changes to your requests or response handling.\"]}]\n1fc:[\"$\",\"li\",\"17\",{\"children\":[\"Like Claude Fable 5, both models require 30-day data retention and aren’t available under zero data retention unless expressly authorized by Anthropic. See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/manage-claude/api-and-data-retention#model-specific-data-retention-requirements\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Model-specific data retention requirements\"]}],\".\"]}]\n1fd:[\"$\",\"li\",\"19\",{\"children\":[\"The guides for the \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/api/beta/organization\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Claude Enterprise endpoints of the Admin API\"]}],\" (\",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/manage-claude/user-management\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"user management\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/manage-claude/spend-limits-api\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"spend limits\"]}],\"), the \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/manage-claude/analytics-api\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Claude Enterprise Analytics API\"]}],\", and the \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"9\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/manage-claude/compliance-api\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Compliance API\"]}],\" now show the \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"11\",{\"children\":[\"anthropic-version\"]}],\" header; send it on every request to these endpoints, as in the rest of the Claude API. See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"13\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/api/versioning\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"API versions\"]}],\".\"]}]\n1fe:[\"$\",\"code\",\"1\",{\"children\":[\"skills-2025-10-02\"]}]\n1ff:[\"$\",\"li\",\"11\",{\"children\":[\"The \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/api/beta/organization\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Admin API user-management endpoints\"]}],\" for \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"Claude Enterprise\"]}],\" (claude.ai) organizations (members, invites, groups, and custom roles) are out of beta. The \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"anthropic-beta: ce-user-management-2026-07-13\"]}],\" header is no longer required on group and custom-role requests; requests that still send it are accepted unchanged. See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/manage-claude/user-management\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"User management\"]}],\".\"]}]\n200:[\"$\",\"li\",\"13\",{\"children\":[\"You can now restrict which sites a Claude Managed Agents agent’s \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"1\",{\"children\":[\"web_search\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"web_fetch\"]}],\" tools can reach. Set \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"allowed_domains\"]}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"7\",{\"children\":[\"blocked_domains\"]}],\" on the tool’s entry in the \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"9\",{\"children\":[\"agent_toolset_20260401\"]}],\" \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"11\",{\"children\":[\"configs\"]}],\" array; \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"13\",{\"children\":[\"web_fetch\"]}],\" also accepts \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"15\",{\"children\":[\"max_content_tokens\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"17\",{\"children\":[\"web_search\"]}],\" accepts \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"19\",{\"children\":[\"user_location\"]}],\". Each \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"21\",{\"children\":[\"configs\"]}],\" entry is identified by its \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"23\",{\"children\":[\"name\"]}],\" and typed by an optional \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"25\",{\"children\":[\"type\"]}],\", and requests that pass only \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"27\",{\"children\":[\"name\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"29\",{\"children\":[\"enabled\"]}],\", and \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"31\",{\"children\":[\"permission_policy\"]}],\" continue to work; in the typed SDKs, \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"33\",{\"children\":[\"configs\"]}],\" entries become \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"35\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/tools#config-entry-types-in-the-sdks\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"per-tool types\"]}],\". See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"37\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/tools-web-restrictions\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Restrict web search and web fetch domains\"]}],\".\"]}]\n201:[\"$\",\"li\",\"15\",{\"children\":[\"Claude Managed Agents sessions that run in a \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/self-hosted-sandboxes\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"self-hosted sandbox\"]}],\" can now attach \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/memory\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"memory stores\"]}],\". The Python, TypeScript, and Go SDK workers download each attached store into the sandbox at its \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"mount_path\"]}],\" and sync the agent’s changes back to the store. See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/self-hosted-sandboxes-memory\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Memory stores in self-hosted sandboxes\"]}],\".\"]}]\n202:[\"$\",\"li\",\"17\",{\"children\":[\"The session viewer in the Claude Console has been redesigned with a timeline minimap, a transcript grouped by model request, and an Inspector panel for session details and cost, raw events, per-tool statistics, mounted resources, and per-thread activity. See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/session-observability#inspect-a-session-in-the-console\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Inspect a session in the Console\"]}],\".\"]}]\n203:[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/models/opus-5/overview\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Claude Opus 5\"]}]\n204:[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"9\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/build-with-claude/fast-mode#supported-models\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Fast mode model availability\"]}]\n206:[\"$\",\"li\",\"11\",{\"children\":[\"Webhooks for Claude Managed Agents now cover the agent, deployment, and deployment run lifecycle. You can react to a newly published agent version, a paused deployment, or a failed scheduled run without polling. See the Agent events, Deployment events, and Deployment run events tabs in \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/webhooks#supported-event-types\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Supported event types\"]}],\".\"]}]\n207:[\"$\",\"li\",\"13\",{\"children\":[\"Claude Fable 5 requires 30-day data retention and is not available under zero data retention. See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/manage-claude/api-and-data-retention#model-specific-data-retention-requirements\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Model-specific data retention requirements\"]}],\".\"]}]\n208:[\"$\",\"li\",\"15\",{\"children\":[\"Claude Managed Agents now supports \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/scheduled-deployments\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"scheduled deployments\"]}],\", letting you run sessions on a cron schedule without managing your own scheduler.\"]}]\n209:[\"$\",\"li\",\"17\",{\"children\":[\"Claude Managed Agents vaults now support \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/vaults#add-a-credential\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"environment variable credentials\"]}],\", so you can securely inject secrets into the agent’s sandbox for CLIs, SDKs, and other services that authenticate through environment variables.\"]}]\n20a:[\"$\",\"li\",\"19\",{\"children\":[\"The \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/manage-claude/compliance-api\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Compliance API\"]}],\" \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/manage-claude/compliance-activity-feed\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Activity Feed\"]}],\" (\",[\"$\",\"code\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"GET /v1/compliance/activities\"]}],\") is now available on \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/build-with-claude/claude-platform-on-aws\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Claude Platform on AWS\"]}],\". See \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"9\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/api/claude-platform-on-aws-iam-actions#compliance\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Compliance IAM actions for Claude Platform on AWS\"]}],\" for the \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"11\",{\"children\":[\"ListComplianceActivities\"]}],\" action that authorizes it.\"]}]\n20b:[\"$\",\"li\",\"21\",{\"children\":[\"The \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"1\",{\"children\":[\"session.thread_*\"]}],\" webhook events now include a \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"session_thread_id\"]}],\" field identifying the multiagent thread that triggered the event.\"]}]\n20c:[\"$\",\"li\",\"23\",{\"children\":[\"We’ve released a \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/cli-sdks-libraries/libraries/apple-foundation-models\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Swift package\"]}],\" in beta that adds Claude as a server-side \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"LanguageModel\"]}],\" in Apple’s Foundation Models framework. Call Claude through the same \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"LanguageModelSession\"]}],\" API as Apple’s on-device model on iOS 27, macOS 27, visionOS 27, and watchOS 27 (beta).\"]}]\n20e:[\"$\",\"code\",\"1\",{\"children\":[\"temperature\"]}]\n20f:[\"$\",\"code\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"top_p\"]}]\n210:[\"$\",\"code\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"top_k\"]}]\n211:[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/about-claude/models/migration-guide\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"migration guide\"]}]\n212:[\"$\",\"li\",\"25\",{\"children\":[\"In Claude Code, we’ve expanded Auto mode to more users for long-running tasks. See the \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"https://code.claude.com/docs\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Claude Code documentation\"]}],\".\"]}]\n213:[\"$\",\"li\",\"27\",{\"children\":[\"In Claude Code, Max plan users now default to \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/build-with-claude/fast-mode\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"fast mode\"]}],\" on Claude Opus 4.8. See the \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"https://code.claude.com/docs\",\"untracked\":false,\"children\":[\"Claude Code documentation\"]}],\".\"]}]\n214:[\"$\",\"li\",\"29\",{\"children\":[\"In Claude Code, Workflows are available as a research preview, letting you define and run multistep agentic plans. See the \",[\"$\",\"$L97\",\"1\",{\"href\